{"title":"2025 TMTA High School Algebra I Contest Problems/Problem 9","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_I_Contest_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>What is the greatest common factor (GCF) of the terms in the polynomial\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/d/22dbaee9646fd1874d8a280c0bf7a007e55a17b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${88a^4b^2+16a^3b-144a^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"184\" height=\"18\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/3/f530685474a0bfebc65154b006170d9d00d314c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\  4a \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\  8ab \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\  8a^2 \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\  16a^2 \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\  16a^4 \\qquad$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"481\" height=\"21\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_I_Contest_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>All of the terms have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/3/373f3e9c1a9cba15c65e133604eb42156015afe2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^{2}$\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> since all of them have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> with a power of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> or greater, though <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> isn't in the prime factorization. Additionally, all coefficients are divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/7/ac7a8407d6b9036375d717ae9cdd1f966ce0c4a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{88}{8} = 11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"66\" height=\"38\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/4/354dfb18aa99a56db016ec2a02d680d82202c907.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{16}{8} = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"57\" height=\"38\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/b/59b47879a96ef9fac4c64ab2e43887673e36adcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{144}{8} = 18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"76\" height=\"38\" />. However, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is prime, so this cannot be divided further. Thus, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/5/72533f6c586c0b088ec6f50b8e85f4fdc284e447.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf {(C) } 8a^{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"74\" height=\"32\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_I_Contest\" title=\"2025 TMTA High School Algebra I Contest\">2025 TMTA Algebra I</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_I_Contest_Problems\" title=\"2025 TMTA High School Algebra I Contest Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_I_Contest_Answer_Key\" title=\"2025 TMTA High School Algebra I Contest Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_I_Contest_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2025 TMTA High School Algebra I Contest Problems/Problem 8\">Problem 8</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_I_Contest_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2025 TMTA High School Algebra I Contest Problems/Problem 10\">Problem 10</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_I_Contest_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2025 TMTA High School Algebra I Contest Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_I_Contest_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2025 TMTA High School Algebra I Contest Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_I_Contest_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2025 TMTA High School Algebra I Contest Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_I_Contest_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2025 TMTA High School Algebra I Contest Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_I_Contest_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2025 TMTA High School Algebra I Contest Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_I_Contest_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2025 TMTA High School Alg